  "summary": "M2 is the pile of US dollars in cash, checking, savings, small CDs, and retail money-market funds. Right now it is about $23.2 trillion. That is a stock of money, not a year's spending. Compared with one year of world output (World Bank, 2025), it is roughly 20% \u2014 a size check, not a slice of global M2. The Fed changed the M2 recipe in 2020, so treat the level around that year with care.",
